  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The empirical validation of the model is limited to a single agribusiness case study over a short 10-day campaign period.",
      "what": "This study develops a Petri Net-based decision-support model to simulate agricultural supply chain operations under disruptive conditions in Ukraine. Tested on an agribusiness case study, the model defines five operational threshold regimes and evaluates fleet-sizing configurations for 13-hour and 16-hour service level agreements. Empirical validation over 10 campaign days demonstrated high predictive accuracy, yielding a Mean Absolute Error of 0.44 hours and a Mean Absolute Percentage Error of 2.73%.",
      "why": "It provides agricultural enterprises with a quantitative tool to balance harvesting and transport capacities, preventing 'transport-collapse' bottlenecks where adding harvesting equipment without sufficient trucking actually increases shipping times from 11.8 to over 19 hours."
    }
  },
